# Go style and SOLID (user-agent)

When editing Go in this repository:

1. Read and apply `.agents/skills/google-go-style-guide/SKILL.md` (and guide/style-decisions as needed).
2. Read and apply `.agents/skills/solid-go-design/SKILL.md`.

## Local norms

- Format with `gofmt`; keep lines within golines max-len 80 (see `.golangci.yml`).
- Use stdlib `testing` only; failure messages put **got before want**.
- Prefer MixedCaps; avoid package names that collide with the standard library.
- Do not add speculative interfaces. Keep `detect.Detector` as a single method.
- Wire the detector pipeline only in `useragent` (composition root); do not create
  `detect` → subpackage → `detect` import cycles.
- Detectors fill empty fields unless they own the concern; Client Hints merge may
  overwrite. Preserve documented order: bot → app → agent → engine → opsys →
  device → merge.
- Avoid new package-level mutable client state; prefer `Analyzer` at call sites
  when customization or tests need isolation.
